F-1 (Foxy portability): pick the typesupport idiom by capability, not by name.

Upstream branches on `DISTRO_ROS STREQUAL "humble" OR "jazzy"` to choose
between rosidl_get_typesupport_target() (Galactic+) and the older
add_dependencies + get_target_property form. colcon.pkg (patch 0005) carries
one fixed -DDISTRO_ROS value, but this tree is built on BOTH Humble and Foxy —
the G1's onboard computer runs Foxy — so on Foxy the humble value selects a
branch calling a macro that does not exist there.

Gating on `if(COMMAND rosidl_get_typesupport_target)` picks the same branch
upstream intended on every distro, and makes DISTRO_ROS irrelevant to this
decision. The else() branch is upstream's own, unchanged.

Applies on top of patches 0005 + 0008.
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -282,7 +282,12 @@
   target_include_directories(${PROJECT_NAME} PRIVATE ${livox_sdk_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 
   # get include directories of custom msg headers
-  if(DISTRO_ROS STREQUAL "humble" OR DISTRO_ROS STREQUAL "jazzy")
+  # Gate on the command, not on the DISTRO_ROS string: colcon.pkg carries one
+  # fixed -DDISTRO_ROS value but this tree is built on both Humble and Foxy
+  # (the G1's onboard PC), and `humble` there would take a branch calling a
+  # macro Foxy does not define. rosidl_get_typesupport_target() is Galactic+;
+  # the else() branch below is the pre-Galactic equivalent.
+  if(COMMAND rosidl_get_typesupport_target)
     rosidl_get_typesupport_target(cpp_typesupport_target
     ${LIVOX_INTERFACES} "rosidl_typesupport_cpp")
     target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME} "${cpp_typesupport_target}")
